	//
	// Loads `kind` (`image`, `video`, or `web`) onto the monitors listed in
	// `targets`. If `targets` is omitted or empty, the wallpaper is applied to
	// all connected monitors.
	//
	// The server responds `200` only after every targeted monitor reaches a
	// terminal state (`applied`, `superseded`, or `failed`), or after
	// `loadAckTimeoutMs` (10 s) elapses, in which case any monitor that never
	// reported is recorded as `timeout`. This makes the acknowledgement
	// truthful: the caller can tell from `ok` and each target's `outcome`
